From 6780996f8606b5546f5422ac510dea29d237b106 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:53:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] test(stepped_stock_rapid): a coarse stock of deleted source
 is refused by the fidelity clause first

Since PR #1127 (#1056) a FromModel stock carries its source's chord, so
the coarse casting deleted from the tree is refused by the fidelity
clause, which runs first in the post gate by design (#864) and silences
the sim's lines (#1056 point 3). The refusal order did not change; the
test still expected the rapid law to be the one named.

a_coarse_stock_whose_source_is_gone_is_never_acquitted now asserts the
post is blocked by the coarse-import refusal by name, that the rapid law
still convicts the dive (RapidInStock), and that the exact-and-deleted
twin is blocked by the rapid law by name. Decision in
docs/decisions/1336-coarse-refusal-first.md.

Fixes #1336

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
